---
import FeaturesLayout from '../../layouts/FeaturesLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<FeaturesLayout
  currentSlug="usage"
  title="Usage — compodocx command patterns for Angular docs"
  description="compodocx command patterns: one-shot CI builds, watch + live-reload, multi-version output, npm scripts integration, semver-aware API diffs in CI."
>
  <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary text-lg">
    A few patterns we lean on. Every flag has a JSON-config equivalent.
  </p>

  <h2>Build once for CI</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code="npx compodocx -p tsconfig.doc.json" />
  <p>
    Writes to <code class="cdx-code">./documentation/&lt;versionLabel&gt;/</code> by default. The label
    is read from the nearest <code class="cdx-code">package.json</code>. Pass
    <code class="cdx-code">--no-multiVersion</code> for a flat output.
  </p>

  <h2>Watch during authoring</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code="npx compodocx -p tsconfig.doc.json --watch --serve" />
  <p>
    The dev server reuses the same routing and theming as production. What you see locally matches
    what ships.
  </p>

  <h2>Multi-version with a custom label</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code="npx compodocx -p tsconfig.doc.json --versionLabel v1.4.0" />
  <p>
    Writes <code class="cdx-code">./documentation/v1.4.0/</code> and updates
    <code class="cdx-code">./documentation/versions.json</code>. The manifest is append-only,
    deduplicated by label, and semver-sorted descending. The version-switcher in the navbar reads it
    at runtime, no extra wiring.
  </p>

  <h2>
    Wire into <a
      href="https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v10/using-npm/scripts"
      rel="noopener"
      target="_blank"
      class="text-cdx-primary underline-offset-2 hover:underline"
      >npm scripts<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span></a
    >
  </h2>
  <CodeBlock
    lang="json"
    filename="package.json"
    code={`"docs": "compodocx -p tsconfig.doc.json",
"docs:watch": "compodocx -p tsconfig.doc.json --watch --serve",
"docs:json": "compodocx -p tsconfig.doc.json --exportFormat json -d snapshots/",
"docs:llm": "compodocx -p tsconfig.doc.json --exportFormat llm-md"`}
  />

  <h2>API diff between snapshots</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    lang="bash"
    code={`npx compodocx -p tsconfig.doc.json --exportFormat json -d snapshots/next/
npx compodocx diff snapshots/prev/<label>/api.json snapshots/next/<label>/api.json`}
  />
  <p>
    Exits <code class="cdx-code">0</code> on no public-API change,
    <code class="cdx-code">1</code> on additive changes, <code class="cdx-code">2</code> on breaking changes
    (or fatal errors). Pipe the JSON output to your bot of choice for PR comments.
  </p>

  <h2>LLM context for code review</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code="npx compodocx -p tsconfig.doc.json --exportFormat llm-md" />
  <p>
    Without <code class="cdx-code">-d</code>, writes to stdout. Pipe straight into
    <code class="cdx-code">llm</code>, <code class="cdx-code">claude</code>, or any tool that reads
    markdown. With <code class="cdx-code">-d</code>, writes
    <code class="cdx-code">&lt;output&gt;/llm-context.md</code>.
  </p>
</FeaturesLayout>
